  <h1>About Daily Insight Desk</h1>
  <p class="dek">A small home-and-garden desk for readers in the United States. The promise is a clear answer to a real chore, not a pile of products.</p>
  <p>Daily Insight Desk is operated by Etern Digital. The site used to be a short list of product picks. It is now a guide to cleaning, the kitchen, the yard, and the tools those jobs share. The audience is American households, and the writing is in American English.</p>
  <h2>How a guide gets written</h2>
  <p>We start with the task: unclog a nozzle, choose a board, rinse a patio, put tools away dry. We say what the job needs, what it does not need, and where a product is only one option. If a claim comes from a manufacturer, we call it a seller’s claim. If it comes from another publication, we name the publication and link it. If we have not used the product, we do not describe a test we did not run.</p>
  <p>We do not publish invented statistics, fabricated testimonials, or medical claims. A cutting board guide can talk about washing a board. It cannot tell you a surface will keep you healthy.</p>
  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>Some links are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we may earn a commission, and the price you pay is the seller’s price. Those links use <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. The note sits near the top of a guide, not in a footer you never see. Editorial choices are not a receipt for the commission. A product can be mentioned with a clear limitation, including “this is the wrong tool for the job you think you are buying it for.”</p>
  <p>The full terms are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. Questions about an order, a refund, or a shipment belong to the store that took the payment. We do not have those records.</p>
  <h2>What is not here yet</h2>
  <p>Most of the guide list is still ahead. Shelf pages name those upcoming pieces and do not link them, so you are never sent to a missing page. A newsletter is planned and is not open. We are not collecting email addresses until there is a letter to send.</p>
  <h2>Write to us</h2>
  <p>Corrections are welcome. If a sentence is wrong, say so. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>, or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
